flowchart LR
accTitle: A wallet authorizes a separate app key
accDescr: The browser generates an app key. The custody wallet approves that key’s public identity and limited permissions. A signed KEY_ADD is submitted and confirmed, after which the app key can sign everyday actions. Neither private key is sent to the server.
subgraph B["Your browser or wallet · private keys stay here"]
 key["1 · Create an app key"]:::device
 wallet["2 · Custody wallet approves"]:::device
 everyday["4 · App key signs everyday posts"]:::done
end
subgraph S["Your server + Farcaster network"]
 registered["3 · Register and confirm KEY_ADD"]:::data
end
key -->|"Public key + permissions"| wallet
wallet -->|"Signed authorization · no gas"| registered
registered -->|"Key is active"| everyday
